            <ArticleTitle>Student life - What it's like to be a gay male nursing student.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>35</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.7748/ns.31.23.35.s40</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>I trained as a nurse in the 1980s, when societal attitudes towards gay people were less tolerant than they are today. I was open about being gay with colleagues and friends throughout my nurse training and subsequent career, and I never experienced homophobia - but I know that others have.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
